feat(tool-market): judge_setup — adjudicate a proposal, never invent one

The judgment layer was the missing piece: three perceptual layers existed but
nothing assembled them into his AND-gate.

The contract is inverted on purpose. His T1/T2/T3 derivation is closed-source and
the corpus reconstruction doc rates 'derive T1/T2 from ATR' a HIGH-severity error,
so this tool does not compute targets: the caller proposes entry, stop and targets
and the tool adjudicates — the same posture as audit_backtest.

Gates, each with the rule it enforces:

- three-piece: entry, stop and target must arrive together; a missing leg is a
  veto, not a soft score.
- alignment: two timeframes must agree on trend direction; the gate may only
  forbid, never pick a side.
- direction: the regime decides what an extreme means, so fading an oversold in a
  trend baseline is vetoed (green = continuation, not reversal).
- structure: the entry must sit within 1 ATR of a confirmed fractal level or it is
  adrift; a fresh extreme has no level by construction and says so.
- risk-reward: rr per target, T1 must clear 1:1, stop on the right side.
- cross-asset: veto only, and only under a caller-supplied threshold — a stretched
  ratio can stay stretched, so no rule is assumed.
- unavailable: momentum countdown, cross-instrument ranking, his channel and fund
  flow are reported UNKNOWN and never silently passed; a substantive unknown
  forces STAND ASIDE.

33 test files, 543 tests.